/-!
# A standard étale algebra maps into a finite flat cover, prime by prime

Let `R → S` be a standard étale ring map, presented as `S = R[x]_g/(f)` with `f` monic. This file
proves Stacks 00UF: there is one finite, finitely presented, faithfully flat `R`-algebra `S'` such
that whenever a prime `q ⊂ S` and a prime `q' ⊂ S'` lie over the same prime of `R` there are a
`g' ∈ S'`, `g' ∉ q'`, and an `R`-algebra map `φ : S → S'_{g'}` with `φ⁻¹(q'S'_{g'}) = q`.

The cover is the one of Lemma 03HS: a finite free faithfully flat extension `R → S'` in which
`f = ∏_{i} (x - β_i)`. Each root gives an `R`-algebra map `R[x]/(f) → S'`, and the whole content of
the lemma is that for a suitable root the induced map has `q` as the contraction of `q'`. The proof
here reads that off the residue fields. Write `κ(p)`, `κ(q)`, `κ(q')` for the residue fields at
`p = q ∩ R = q' ∩ R` and at `q`, `q'`; then `κ(q)` and `κ(q')` are extensions of `κ(p)`, and `κ(q)`
is generated over `κ(p)` by the image `x̄` of `x`, because every element of `S` becomes
`p(x)g(x)^{-n}` in `S` and `g(x)` is invertible. As `x̄` is annihilated by the monic `f` and `f`
splits in `κ(q')`, the minimal polynomial of `x̄` splits there too, so `κ(q)` embeds into `κ(q')`
over `κ(p)`. Composing gives an `R`-algebra map `χ : S → κ(q')` whose kernel is `q`. Its value
`χ(x)` is a root of `f` in `κ(q')`, hence is the image of some `β_i`, and `χ(g(x))` is a unit; so
`g' := g(β_i)` is not in `q'`, and the map `φ : S → S'_{g'}` sending `x` to `β_i` composes with
`S'_{g'} → κ(q')` to give `χ`. Therefore `φ⁻¹(q'S'_{g'}) = χ⁻¹(0) = q`, the first equality because
the kernel of `S'_{g'} → κ(q')` is `q'S'_{g'}`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Etale.FiniteFlatDomination.solution`: Stacks 00UF, the statement of
  `Algebra.IsStandardEtale.exists_finite_faithfullyFlat_forall_exists_comp_eq_comap_eq`.

## Implementation notes

The residue field `κ(p)` is Mathlib's `Ideal.ResidueField`, which comes with
`IsFractionRing (R ⧸ p) p.ResidueField` and with the embedding `κ(p) → κ(q)` of
`Ideal.ResidueField.mapₐ`; the latter is not an instance, so the `κ(p)`-algebra structures on
`κ(q)` and on `κ(q')` are installed locally inside the proof.

Three steps are isolated as private lemmas: that the kernel of the lift of a ring map to a
localization is the ideal generated by the kernel (`ker_isLocalization_lift`); that a simple
extension whose generator is annihilated by a monic polynomial splitting in a second extension
embeds into it (`nonempty_algHom_of_adjoin_singleton_eq_top`); and that `κ(q)` is generated over
`κ(p)` by the image of the coordinate of a standard étale presentation
(`adjoin_singleton_residueField_eq_top`). The last is the only one that uses the presentation, via
`StandardEtalePresentation.exists_mul_aeval_x_g_pow_eq_aeval_x`, and it is stated for an arbitrary
field `κ(p) ⊆ K ⊆ κ(q)` receiving `R`, since no property of `K` beyond that is used.

## References

* [StacksProject 00UF](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00UF), Lemma 10.144.5.
* [StacksProject 03HS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03HS), the finite free faithfully flat
  extension in which a monic polynomial splits.
* [StacksProject 00UB](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00UB), standard étale ring maps.
-/



namespace Stacks.Etale.FiniteFlatDomination

open Polynomial

/-- The kernel of the lift of `g : A →+* L` to a localization `B` of `A` at `M`, where `g` sends
`M` to units, is the ideal generated by the kernel of `g`. -/
private lemma ker_isLocalization_lift {A B L : Type*} [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [CommRing L]
    [Algebra A B] (M : Submonoid A) [IsLocalization M B] {g : A →+* L}
    (hg : ∀ y : M, IsUnit (g y)) :
    RingHom.ker (IsLocalization.lift (S := B) hg) = (RingHom.ker g).map (algebraMap A B) := by
  refine le_antisymm (fun b hb ↦ ?_) (Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap.2 fun a ha ↦ ?_)
  · obtain ⟨⟨a, m⟩, hm⟩ := IsLocalization.surj M b
    have hu : IsUnit (algebraMap A B (m : A)) := IsLocalization.map_units B m
    have ha : a ∈ RingHom.ker g := by
      have h := congrArg (IsLocalization.lift (S := B) hg) hm
      rw [map_mul, IsLocalization.lift_eq, IsLocalization.lift_eq, RingHom.mem_ker.1 hb,
        zero_mul] at h
      exact RingHom.mem_ker.2 h.symm
    have hmem : b * algebraMap A B (m : A) ∈ (RingHom.ker g).map (algebraMap A B) := by
      rw [hm]
      exact Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ ha
    rwa [mul_comm, Ideal.unit_mul_mem_iff_mem _ hu] at hmem
  · simp [RingHom.mem_ker, IsLocalization.lift_eq, RingHom.mem_ker.1 ha]

/-- A simple field extension `M = K(x)` embeds over `K` into any extension `L` of `K` in which
some monic polynomial annihilating `x` splits. -/
private lemma nonempty_algHom_of_adjoin_singleton_eq_top {K M L : Type*} [Field K] [Field M]
    [Field L] [Algebra K M] [Algebra K L] {x : M}
    (hx : IntermediateField.adjoin K {x} = ⊤) {F : K[X]} (hF : F.Monic) (hFx : aeval x F = 0)
    (hFL : (F.map (algebraMap K L)).Splits) : Nonempty (M →ₐ[K] L) := by
  have H : IsIntegral K x ∧ ((minpoly K x).map (algebraMap K L)).Splits :=
    ⟨⟨F, hF, hFx⟩, hFL.of_dvd (hF.map (algebraMap K L)).ne_zero
      (Polynomial.map_dvd _ (minpoly.dvd K x hFx))⟩
  refine IntermediateField.nonempty_algHom_of_adjoin_splits (fun s hs ↦ ?_) hx
  obtain rfl : s = x := hs
  exact H

/-- The residue field at a prime `q` of a standard étale algebra `S` is generated, over any field
`K` between `R` and it, by the image of the coordinate of a standard étale presentation. -/
private lemma adjoin_singleton_residueField_eq_top {R S : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing S]
    [Algebra R S] (P : StandardEtalePresentation R S) (q : Ideal S) [q.IsPrime] (K : Type*)
    [Field K] [Algebra R K] [Algebra K q.ResidueField] [IsScalarTower R K q.ResidueField] :
    IntermediateField.adjoin K {algebraMap S q.ResidueField P.x} = ⊤ := by
  have key : ∀ p : R[X], aeval (algebraMap S q.ResidueField P.x) p
      ∈ IntermediateField.adjoin K {algebraMap S q.ResidueField P.x} := by
    intro p
    rw [← Polynomial.aeval_map_algebraMap K]
    exact IntermediateField.algebra_adjoin_le_adjoin K _
      (Polynomial.aeval_mem_adjoin_singleton K _)
  have hgne : aeval (algebraMap S q.ResidueField P.x) P.g ≠ 0 := by
    rw [Polynomial.aeval_algebraMap_apply]
    exact (P.hasMap.2.map (algebraMap S q.ResidueField)).ne_zero
  have hmemS : ∀ y : S, algebraMap S q.ResidueField y
      ∈ IntermediateField.adjoin K {algebraMap S q.ResidueField P.x} := by
    intro y
    obtain ⟨p₀, n, hn⟩ := P.exists_mul_aeval_x_g_pow_eq_aeval_x y
    have h1 := congrArg (algebraMap S q.ResidueField) hn
    rw [map_mul, map_pow, ← Polynomial.aeval_algebraMap_apply,
      ← Polynomial.aeval_algebraMap_apply] at h1
    rw [(eq_div_iff (pow_ne_zero n hgne)).2 h1]
    exact div_mem (key p₀) (pow_mem (key P.g) n)
  have hmemQ : ∀ a : S ⧸ q, algebraMap (S ⧸ q) q.ResidueField a
      ∈ IntermediateField.adjoin K {algebraMap S q.ResidueField P.x} := by
    intro a
    obtain ⟨y, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective a
    rw [Ideal.algebraMap_quotient_residueField_mk]
    exact hmemS y
  rw [eq_top_iff]
  intro z _
  obtain ⟨⟨a, b⟩, hab⟩ := IsLocalization.surj (nonZeroDivisors (S ⧸ q)) z
  have hbne : algebraMap (S ⧸ q) q.ResidueField (b : S ⧸ q) ≠ 0 :=
    (IsLocalization.map_units q.ResidueField b).ne_zero
  rw [(eq_div_iff hbne).2 hab]
  exact div_mem (hmemQ a) (hmemQ b)

/-- A standard étale `R`-algebra `S` maps, prime by prime and after localizing away
from an element, into one finite, finitely presented, faithfully flat `R`-algebra `S'`. This is
the statement of
`Algebra.IsStandardEtale.exists_finite_faithfullyFlat_forall_exists_comp_eq_comap_eq`. -/
public theorem solution
    (R : Type u) [CommRing R] (S : Type v) [CommRing S] [Algebra R S]
    [Algebra.IsStandardEtale R S] :
    ∃ (S' : Type u) (_ : CommRing S') (_ : Algebra R S') (_ : Module.Finite R S')
      (_ : Algebra.FinitePresentation R S') (_ : Module.FaithfullyFlat R S'),
      ∀ (q : Ideal S) (_ : q.IsPrime) (q' : Ideal S') (_ : q'.IsPrime),
        q.under R = q'.under R → ∃ g' ∉ q', ∀ (B : Type w) (_ : CommRing B) (_ : Algebra S' B)
          (_ : IsLocalization.Away g' B), ∃ φ : S →+* B,
            φ.comp (algebraMap R S) = (algebraMap S' B).comp (algebraMap R S') ∧
              (q'.map (algebraMap S' B)).comap φ = q := by
  obtain ⟨P⟩ := Algebra.IsStandardEtale.nonempty_standardEtalePresentation (R := R) (S := S)
  obtain ⟨S', _, _, _, _, _, _, β, hβ⟩ :=
    P.monic_f.exists_finite_free_faithfullyFlat_syntomic_map_eq_prod_X_sub_C
  refine ⟨S', inferInstance, inferInstance, inferInstance, inferInstance, inferInstance, ?_⟩
  intro q hq q' hq' hqq'
  have := hq
  have := hq'
  -- `f` splits in `S'`, hence in the residue field at `q'`, with roots the images of the `β i`
  have hroot : ∀ i, aeval (β i) P.f = 0 := by
    intro i
    have h0 : (P.f.map (algebraMap R S')).eval (β i) = 0 := by
      rw [hβ, Polynomial.eval_prod]
      exact Finset.prod_eq_zero (Finset.mem_univ i) (by simp)
    rwa [Polynomial.eval_map, ← Polynomial.aeval_def] at h0
  have hsplitL : P.f.map (algebraMap R q'.ResidueField)
      = ∏ i, (X - C (algebraMap S' q'.ResidueField (β i))) := by
    have h := congrArg (Polynomial.map (algebraMap S' q'.ResidueField)) hβ
    rw [Polynomial.map_map, ← IsScalarTower.algebraMap_eq] at h
    rw [h, Polynomial.map_prod]
    exact Finset.prod_congr rfl fun i _ ↦ by simp
  -- the residue fields at `q` and at `q'` as extensions of the residue field at `p = q ∩ R`
  let ιM : (q.under R).ResidueField →ₐ[R] q.ResidueField :=
    Ideal.ResidueField.mapₐ (q.under R) q (Algebra.ofId R S) rfl
  let ιL : (q.under R).ResidueField →ₐ[R] q'.ResidueField :=
    Ideal.ResidueField.mapₐ (q.under R) q' (Algebra.ofId R S') hqq'
  let : Algebra (q.under R).ResidueField q.ResidueField := ιM.toRingHom.toAlgebra
  let : Algebra (q.under R).ResidueField q'.ResidueField := ιL.toRingHom.toAlgebra
  have : IsScalarTower R (q.under R).ResidueField q.ResidueField :=
    .of_algebraMap_eq fun r ↦ (ιM.commutes r).symm
  have : IsScalarTower R (q.under R).ResidueField q'.ResidueField :=
    .of_algebraMap_eq fun r ↦ (ιL.commutes r).symm
  -- an `R`-algebra map `χ : S → κ(q')` with kernel `q`
  obtain ⟨ψ⟩ : Nonempty (q.ResidueField →ₐ[(q.under R).ResidueField] q'.ResidueField) := by
    refine nonempty_algHom_of_adjoin_singleton_eq_top
      (adjoin_singleton_residueField_eq_top P q _)
      (F := P.f.map (algebraMap R (q.under R).ResidueField)) (P.monic_f.map _) ?_ ?_
    · have h := Polynomial.aeval_algHom_apply
        (IsScalarTower.toAlgHom R S q.ResidueField) P.x P.f
      simp only [IsScalarTower.coe_toAlgHom'] at h
      rw [Polynomial.aeval_map_algebraMap, h, P.hasMap.1, map_zero]
    · rw [Polynomial.map_map, ← IsScalarTower.algebraMap_eq, hsplitL]
      exact Polynomial.Splits.prod fun i _ ↦ Polynomial.Splits.X_sub_C _
  let χ : S →ₐ[R] q'.ResidueField :=
    (ψ.restrictScalars R).comp (IsScalarTower.toAlgHom R S q.ResidueField)
  have hχ : (χ : S →+* q'.ResidueField)
      = (ψ : q.ResidueField →+* q'.ResidueField).comp (algebraMap S q.ResidueField) := rfl
  have hψinj : Function.Injective (ψ : q.ResidueField →+* q'.ResidueField) := RingHom.injective _
  have hkerψ : RingHom.ker (ψ : q.ResidueField →+* q'.ResidueField) = ⊥ :=
    (RingHom.injective_iff_ker_eq_bot _).1 hψinj
  have hkerχ : RingHom.ker (χ : S →+* q'.ResidueField) = q := by
    rw [hχ, ← RingHom.comap_ker, hkerψ, ← RingHom.ker_eq_comap_bot,
      Ideal.ker_algebraMap_residueField]
  -- `χ x` is one of the roots
  have hbroot : ∏ i, (χ P.x - algebraMap S' q'.ResidueField (β i)) = 0 := by
    have h0 : aeval (χ P.x) P.f = 0 := by
      rw [Polynomial.aeval_algHom_apply, P.hasMap.1, map_zero]
    rw [Polynomial.aeval_def, ← Polynomial.eval_map, hsplitL, Polynomial.eval_prod] at h0
    simpa using h0
  obtain ⟨i, -, hi⟩ := Finset.prod_eq_zero_iff.1 hbroot
  have hbi : χ P.x = algebraMap S' q'.ResidueField (β i) := sub_eq_zero.1 hi
  -- the element `g' = g(β i)`, a nonzero element of `κ(q')`
  have hg'ne : algebraMap S' q'.ResidueField (aeval (β i) P.g) ≠ 0 := by
    rw [← Polynomial.aeval_algebraMap_apply, ← hbi, Polynomial.aeval_algHom_apply]
    exact (P.hasMap.2.map χ).ne_zero
  refine ⟨aeval (β i) P.g, fun hmem ↦ hg'ne (Ideal.algebraMap_residueField_eq_zero.2 hmem), ?_⟩
  intro B _ _ _
  let : Algebra R B := ((algebraMap S' B).comp (algebraMap R S')).toAlgebra
  have : IsScalarTower R S' B := .of_algebraMap_eq' rfl
  have hmapB : P.HasMap (algebraMap S' B (β i)) := by
    refine ⟨?_, ?_⟩
    · rw [Polynomial.aeval_algebraMap_apply, hroot i, map_zero]
    · rw [Polynomial.aeval_algebraMap_apply]
      exact IsLocalization.Away.algebraMap_isUnit _
  let φ : S →ₐ[R] B := (P.lift (algebraMap S' B (β i)) hmapB).comp P.equivRing.toAlgHom
  have hunits : ∀ y : Submonoid.powers (aeval (β i) P.g),
      IsUnit (algebraMap S' q'.ResidueField (y : S')) := by
    rintro ⟨y, n, rfl⟩
    rw [map_pow]
    exact (isUnit_iff_ne_zero.2 hg'ne).pow n
  have hφx : φ P.x = algebraMap S' B (β i) := by
    show (P.lift (algebraMap S' B (β i)) hmapB) (P.equivRing P.x) = _
    rw [P.equivRing_x, StandardEtalePair.lift_X]
  set θ : B →+* q'.ResidueField := IsLocalization.lift hunits with hθdef
  have hθalg : θ.comp (algebraMap R B) = algebraMap R q'.ResidueField := by
    show θ.comp ((algebraMap S' B).comp (algebraMap R S')) = _
    rw [← RingHom.comp_assoc, hθdef, IsLocalization.lift_comp]
    exact (IsScalarTower.algebraMap_eq R S' q'.ResidueField).symm
  let θₐ : B →ₐ[R] q'.ResidueField := AlgHom.mk θ fun r ↦ RingHom.congr_fun hθalg r
  have hcomp : θₐ.comp φ = χ := by
    refine P.hom_ext ?_
    rw [AlgHom.comp_apply, hφx]
    show θ (algebraMap S' B (β i)) = χ P.x
    rw [hθdef, IsLocalization.lift_eq, hbi]
  refine ⟨φ, ?_, ?_⟩
  · rw [AlgHom.comp_algebraMap]
    rfl
  · have hkerθ : RingHom.ker θ = q'.map (algebraMap S' B) := by
      rw [hθdef, ker_isLocalization_lift, Ideal.ker_algebraMap_residueField]
    rw [← hkerθ, RingHom.comap_ker,
      show θ.comp (φ : S →+* B) = (χ : S →+* q'.ResidueField) from congrArg AlgHom.toRingHom hcomp,
      hkerχ]

end Stacks.Etale.FiniteFlatDomination

/-!
# A standard étale algebra is dominated, prime by prime, by a finite flat cover

Let `R → S` be a standard étale ring map, so `S ≅ R[x]_g/(f)` with `f` monic and `f'` invertible
in `S`. Then `R` admits a single finite flat cover `R → S'` — finite, of finite presentation and
faithfully flat, that is, finite projective as an `R`-module and surjective on spectra — through
which `S` maps after a Zariski localization, in the following prime-by-prime sense: whenever a
prime `q ⊂ S` and a prime `q' ⊂ S'` lie over the same prime `p ⊂ R`, there is a `g' ∈ S'` with
`g' ∉ q'` and an `R`-algebra map `φ : S → S'_{g'}` with `φ⁻¹(q'S'_{g'}) = q`. So the étale
topology is coarser than the topology generated by Zariski coverings and finite flat covers.

The source's proof. Take a presentation `S = R[x]_g/(f)` with `f = x^n + a_1x^{n-1} + … + a_n`
monic, and let `R → S'` be a finite free, faithfully flat extension in which `f` splits,
`f = ∏ (x - α_i)` — this is Lemma 03HS, `Polynomial.Monic.exists_splits_map`. The `n` roots give
`n` `R`-algebra maps `φ_i : R[x]/(f) → S'`, `x ↦ α_i`, and one shows that for a suitable `i` the
image of `φ_i(g)` in `κ(q')` is nonzero and `φ_i⁻¹(q') = q`; then `g' = φ_i(g)` and `φ = φ_i`
serve. Indeed `q` corresponds to an irreducible factor `f_1` of the image `f̄` of `f` in
`κ(p)[x]`, and `g ∉ q` says `f_1 ∤ ḡ`; as `f̄` splits completely in `κ(q')[x]` as `∏ (x - ᾱ_i)`,
one may pick `i` with `f_1(ᾱ_i) = 0` and `ḡ(ᾱ_i) ≠ 0`.

The typical instance: `R = ℤ`, `S = ℤ[x]_{2x}/(x² + 1) ≅ ℤ[i][1/2]`, standard étale since the
derivative `2x` is inverted, and `S' = ℤ[i]`, free of rank two over `ℤ`, in which `x² + 1` splits
as `(x - i)(x + i)`. For `p = (5)`, `q = (2 - i)S` and `q' = (2 + i)`, the map `φ` must be complex
conjugation and `g' = -2i ∉ q'`. So the factoring map genuinely depends on `q'` and is not the
localization map `S → S'_{g'}` of a common presentation.

## Main results

* `Algebra.IsStandardEtale.exists_finite_faithfullyFlat_forall_exists_comp_eq_comap_eq`:
  Lemma 00UF.

## Implementation notes

Conditions (1) and (2) of the source are recorded as `Module.Finite R S'`,
`Algebra.FinitePresentation R S'` and `Module.FaithfullyFlat R S'`. Faithful flatness is exactly
flatness together with surjectivity of `Spec(S') → Spec(R)`, which is condition (2)
(`RingHom.FaithfullyFlat.iff_flat_and_comap_surjective`, with
`PrimeSpectrum.comap_surjective_of_faithfullyFlat` for the direction used here), so nothing is
lost by fusing them; and finite, finitely presented and flat is the source's parenthetical "finite
projective as an `R`-module", the projectivity following from flat plus finitely presented. The
source's proof yields more, namely `Module.Free R S'`; only what the statement claims is recorded,
freeness being an artefact of the particular cover the proof builds. No `Nontrivial R` is needed:
for `R = 0` the choice `S' = 0` satisfies every clause.

`S'` is produced in the universe of `R`, since it is built from `R` by splitting a monic
polynomial, exactly as in `Polynomial.Monic.exists_splits_map`, while the localization `S'_{g'}`
is allowed to be any localization of `S'` away from `g'`, in any universe: the conclusion
quantifies over an arbitrary `B` with `[IsLocalization.Away g' B]` rather than naming
`Localization.Away g'`, so that a user may use their own model of it. By uniqueness of
localizations this is equivalent to the statement for `Localization.Away g'`.

"`q` and `q'` lie over the same prime `p ⊂ R`" is the equation `q.under R = q'.under R` between
contractions, rather than a `p` with two `Ideal.LiesOver` hypotheses: `p` is determined by `q`, and
this form is what a user has to hand. The extended ideal `q'S'_{g'}` is `q'.map (algebraMap S' B)`,
a prime of `B` because `g' ∉ q'`.

Faithfulness to [StacksProject 00UF]:

1. No dead hypothesis. `[Algebra.IsStandardEtale R S]` is load-bearing: for `R = k` a field and
   `S = k(x)`, with `q = 0` and any finite faithfully flat `S'` and any `q'`, the ring `S'_{g'}` is
   nonzero, since `g' ∉ q'` and `q'` is prime make `g'` non-nilpotent, and finite dimensional over
   `k`; an `R`-algebra map `k(x) → S'_{g'}` would then be an injection of `k(x)` into it, so no `φ`
   exists. Primality of `q` is load-bearing since `φ⁻¹` of the prime `q'S'_{g'}` is prime, and
   primality of `q'` both makes `q'S'_{g'}` prime and gives "lying over `p`" its meaning.
2. The scalars and the base are the source's. `S'` is an algebra over `R` itself, not over `S` or a
   localization of `R`; finiteness, finite presentation and faithful flatness are all over `R`;
   `g'` is an element of `S'` and `φ` is defined on all of `S`, not on a localization of it.
3. What the source names is pinned. `R → S'` is `algebraMap R S'` and `S' → S'_{g'}` is
   `algebraMap S' B`, and the source's "the ring map `R → S'_{g'}` factors through `φ`" is the
   equation `φ.comp (algebraMap R S) = (algebraMap S' B).comp (algebraMap R S')` between the two
   canonical maps, so `φ` is an `R`-algebra map and not merely a ring map; `φ` is further pinned by
   `φ⁻¹(q'S'_{g'}) = q`. Only `S'`, `g'` and `φ`, which the source also merely asserts to exist,
   are existentially quantified.
4. The instantiation is not degenerate. In the witness `R = ℤ`, `S = ℤ[i][1/2]`, `S' = ℤ[i]`
   recorded above, `S` is not a localization of `R`, `S'` has two primes over `(5)`, and at one of
   them `φ` is complex conjugation. So the conclusion is not the tautology obtained from `S = R`,
   `S' = R`, `φ = id`.

